# Sibling agent sessions use `git worktree add .worktrees/<slug>` (the hot-repo
# convention in the parent CLAUDE.md). Untracked, these show up as embedded git
# repositories, so a `git add -A` stages ANOTHER session's worktree gitlinks into
# your commit — observed 2026-08-04, three of them plus an unrelated README edit.
# 7 of the 19 w2v repos already ignore this; the rest inherit the hazard.
.worktrees/
